  "notes": "Sole: 12-point rounded rectangle 0.260 x 0.100 (R 32 mm) lofted through 8 rings - (z, inset) 0.0000/0.0018 bottom chamfer, 0.0018/0, 0.0060/0, 0.0066/0.0012, 0.0078/0.0012, 0.0084/0, 0.0150/0, 0.0130/0.0025 - so the side wall has two 1.2 mm grooves and the top a 2.5 mm footbed well; 188 triangles.  Upper: crescent between an outer 49 x 42 mm and an inner 41 x 34 mm ellipse centred at z=6 mm, 9 points per arc = 18-point polygon, swept 55 mm on X from x=-0.020 to 0.035.  Both crescent ends sit at z=6 mm, 9 mm inside the sole, so the union welds them; the arch top is z=0.048.  AABB 0.260 x 0.0998 x 0.0480.  One closed shell.  Three slots: above the sole top fabric_blue, except downward-facing tunnel roof below z=0.042 which is cotton_red; inside the footbed well (horizontal faces below the sole top) cotton_red insole; the rest of the sole is rubber.",
